ological\nAlgorithms\nAnimals\nCerebral Cortex/cytology/*physiology\nElectric Stimulation\nElectrophysiology\nFemale\nMale\nModels, Neurological\nModels, Statistical\nNeurons/*physiology\nPatch-Clamp Techniques\nPyramidal Cells/*physiology\nRats","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/query.fcgi?cmd=Retrieve&db=PubMed&dopt=Citation&list_uids=16807345","year":"2006","type":"Journal Article"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Lee2016-ld","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:23:15Z","response_hash":"ba552b2af00dee32","fields":{"title":"Anatomy and function of an excitatory network in the visual cortex","author":"Lee, Wei-Chung Allen and Bonin, Vincent and Reed, Michael and\n             Graham, Brett J and Hood, Greg and Glattfelder, Katie and Clay\n             Reid, R","journal":"Nature","volume":"532","number":"7599","pages":"370--374","year":"2016"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"LitwinKumarDoiron2012","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:23:15Z","response_hash":"1478130a78d092e5","fields":{"author":"Litwin-Kumar, A. and Doiron, B.","title":"Slow dynamics and high variability in balanced cortical networks with clustered connections","journal":"Nat Neurosci","volume":"15","number":"11","pages":"1498-505","keywords":"Action Potentials/physiology\nAnimals\nCerebral Cortex/*cytology\nCluster Analysis\nComputer Simulation\nHumans\n*Models, Neurological\nNerve Net/*physiology\nNeurons/*physiology\n*Nonlinear Dynamics","issn":"1546-1726 (Electronic)\n1097-6256 (Linking)","doi":"10.1038/nn.3220","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23001062","year":"2012","type":"Journal Article"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"MSR1973dmft","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:23:15Z","response_hash":"1478130a78d092e5","fields":{"title":"Statistical Dynamics of Classical Systems","author":"Martin, P. C. and Siggia, E. D. and Rose, H. A.","journal":"Phys. Rev. A","volume":"8","issue":"1","pages":"423--437","numpages":"0","year":"1973","month":"Jul","publisher":"American Physical Society","doi":"10.1103/PhysRevA.8.423","url":"https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PhysRevA.8.423"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Mascaro1999","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:23:15Z","response_hash":"a93438595101601b","fields":{"author":"Mascaro, M. and Amit, D. J.","title":"Effective neural response function for collective population states","journal":"Network","volume":"10","number":"4","pages":"351-73","keywords":"Animals\nBrain/*physiology\nComputer Simulation\nLearning/physiology\nMemory/physiology\n*Models, Neurological\nNerve Net/*physiology\nNeurons/*physiology\nSynapses/*physiology","issn":"0954-898X (Print)\n0954-898X (Linking)","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10695764","year":"1999","type":"Journal Article"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"MattiaSanchezVives2012","verdict":"partial","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:23:15Z","response_hash":"1478130a78d092e5","fields":{"author":"Mattia, M. and Sanchez-Vives, M. V.","title":"Exploring the spectrum of dynamical regimes and timescales in spontaneous cortical activity","journal":"Cogn Neurodyn","volume":"6","number":"3","pages":"239-50","issn":"1871-4080 (Print)","doi":"10.1007/s11571-011-9179-4","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23730355","year":"2012","type":"Journal Article"},"diffs":[{"field":"year","in_document":"2012","in_source":"2011","severity":"medium"}]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Perin2011-ts","verdict":"verified","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:23:15Z","response_hash":"14828e3ba859f8d8","fields":{"title":"A synaptic organizing principle for cortical neuronal groups","author":"Perin, Rodrigo and Berger, Thomas K and Markram, Henry","abstract":"Neuronal circuitry is often considered a clean slate that can be\n              dynamically and arbitrarily molded by experience. However, when\n              we investigated synaptic connectivity in groups of pyramidal\n              neurons in the neocortex, we found that both connectivity and\n              synaptic weights were surprisingly predictable. Synaptic weights\n              follow very closely the number of connections in a group of\n              neurons, saturating after only 20\\% of possible connections are\n              formed between neurons in a group. When we examined the network\n              topology of connectivity between neurons, we found that the\n              neurons cluster into small world networks that are not\n              scale-free, with less than 2 degrees of separation. We found a\n              simple clustering rule where connectivity is directly\n              proportional to the number of common neighbors, which accounts\n              for these small world networks and accurately predicts the\n              connection probability between any two neurons. This pyramidal\n              neuron network clusters into multiple groups of a few dozen\n              neurons each. The neurons composing each group are surprisingly\n              distributed, typically more than 100 $\\mu$m apart, allowing for\n              multiple groups to be interlaced in the same space. In summary,\n              we discovered a synaptic organizing principle that groups neurons\n              in a manner that is common across animals and hence, independent\n              of individual experiences. We speculate that these elementary\n              neuronal groups are prescribed Lego-like building blocks of\n              perception and that acquired memory relies more on combining\n              these elementary assemblies into higher-order constructs.","journal":"Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. U. S. A.","volume":"108","number":"13","pages":"5419--5424","month":"mar","year":"2011","language":"en"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Sompolinsky1982EAmodel","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:23:15Z","response_hash":"1478130a78d092e5","fields":{"title":"Relaxational dynamics of the Edwards-Anderson model and the mean-field theory of spin-glasses","author":"Sompolinsky, H. and Zippelius, Annette","journal":"Phys. Rev. B","volume":"25","issue":"11","pages":"6860--6875","numpages":"0","year":"1982","month":"Jun","publisher":"American Physical Society","doi":"10.1103/PhysRevB.25.6860","url":"https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PhysRevB.25.6860"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Sompolinsky1987langevin","verdict":"verified","source":"openalex","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:23:15Z","response_hash":"1478130a78d092e5","fields":{"title":"Dynamics of spin systems with randomly asymmetric bonds: Langevin dynamics and a spherical model","author":"Crisanti, A. and Sompolinsky, H.","journal":"Phys. Rev. A","volume":"36","issue":"10","pages":"4922--4939","numpages":"0","year":"1987","month":"Nov","publisher":"American Physical Society","doi":"10.1103/PhysRevA.36.4922","url":"https://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PhysRevA.36.4922"},"diffs":[]},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"Song2005-mj","verdict":"unverified","source":"none","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:23:15Z","response_hash":"","fields":{"title":"Highly nonrandom features of synaptic connectivity in local\n              cortical circuits","author":"Song, Sen and Sj{\\"},"diffs":[],"failure_note":"not found at the registries — books published before DOIs often are not registered; the entry may still be correct"},{"kind":"bib-entry","target":"ahamed2021capturing","verdict":"partial","source":"crossref-query","fetched_at":"2026-09-12T00:23:15Z","response_hash":"7bfc573efbf5b483","fields":{"title":"Capturing the continuous complexity of behaviour in Caenorhabditis elegans","author":"Ahamed, Tosif and Costa, Antonio C and Stephens, Greg J","journal":"Nature Physics","volume":"17","number":"2","pages":"275--283","year":"2021","publisher":"Nature Publishing G